Source: homelab-roundcube
Section: mail
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Jeff Gardner <mailmasker-api01@forge.name>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/homelab

Package: homelab-roundcube
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, roundcube-core, roundcube-pgsql, php-fpm, nginx, adduser, postgresql-client, homelab-common
Recommends: homelab-sso, homelab-dovecot, homelab-postfix, homelab-agent
Description: Roundcube webmail wired to the homelab-* shared identity
 Roundcube webmail (Debian's own roundcube-core/roundcube-pgsql, not
 vendored source). Login is delegated to homelab-sso (Roundcube's own
 native OAuth2 support, plus two small core patches -- see
 script/homelab-roundcube-patch-oauth-sso) -- IMAP authenticates via a
 real XOAUTH2 exchange, not a cached password, and a live homelab-sso
 IdP session lets a user land here already logged in. A plain password
 form (real IMAP LOGIN against homelab-dovecot) remains as a visible
 fallback. Either way, unlike homelab-dovecot/homelab-postfix's narrow
 api.users Postgres grants, this package never touches api.users at
 all -- it proves the unified cross-feature identity design described
 in CLAUDE.md from the browser's side: the same Argon2id-hashed
 password (or, now, the same SSO session) that authenticates IMAP,
 SMTP submission, and homelab-drive's HTTP login also logs into
 webmail, with zero additional credential plumbing.
 .
 Roundcube's own state (contacts, preferences, message cache -- never
 mail itself, which stays entirely in Dovecot's Maildir storage) lives
 in its own "roundcube" Postgres schema via the standard split runtime/
 migrate role pair (script homelab-bootstrap-app-role, the same generic
 tool homelab-api/homelab-drive use -- hence the hard Depends on
 homelab-common above, which is where that tool actually lives; found
 missing on a fresh install, same class of gap already fixed for
 homelab-database/homelab-pgbouncer/homelab-postfix) -- unlike homelab-dovecot's and
 homelab-postfix's bespoke single-role scripts, since Roundcube
 genuinely owns tables and fits the standard two-role pattern. A
 one-time search_path redirect (see script/homelab-roundcube-apply-
 schema) works around Roundcube's vendor code issuing entirely
 unqualified SQL, so its tables land in "roundcube" rather than
 "public".
 .
 Ships its own internal-only nginx+PHP-FPM vhost (loopback only) so
 homelab-webproxy's existing HTTP-upstream reverse-proxy model --
 designed around already-HTTP-speaking backends like homelab-drive's
 hypnotoad -- needs no changes to serve a PHP application.
 .
 homelab-dovecot/homelab-postfix are Recommends, not hard Depends
 (corrected from an earlier version of this package that hard-depended
 on both, conflating "needs a working IMAP/SMTP service" with "needs
 that service's package installed on this same host"): imap_host/
 imap_port/smtp_host/smtp_port (debconf, default localhost) point this
 app at wherever those actually run -- this project's own production
 mail stack, and this ecosystem's own test topology, both routinely run
 Roundcube on a different host from Dovecot/Postfix. Installing this
 package on a host that also happens to run Dovecot/Postfix locally
 (the co-located default) is still fully supported, just no longer
 required.
